<title>SWEDEN: Astra sees Naropin becoming a key drug.</title>
<headline>Astra sees Naropin becoming a key drug.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drug company Astra AB said on Thursday its anaesthetic Naropin would surpass Xylocain in sales and importance within five to 10 years.</p>
<p>&quot;We estimate that Naropin will be a bigger product than Xylocain within five to 10 years,&quot; Astra managing director Hakan Mogren told a seminar in Stockholm.</p>
<p>Xylocain is currently Astra's fifth largest product and sales totalled two billion crowns in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Joel Dahlberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1011</p>
